What each function receives:

A phplyr helper passed as a first-class callable, such as mean(...), is called with the column name.
In summarize(), other closures receive the column’s values as a list.
In mutate(), other closures receive one value at a time, or the whole column if the first parameter is typed array.
A closure may return a helper’s result, as in fn ($v) =&gt; mean($v, naRm: true), which is then evaluated on the group.

Inside any of these functions, cur_column() returns the name of the column being processed.
if_any(cols, fn) and if_all(cols, fn) test a predicate across columns, in filter() or as a logical column in mutate(). They use R’s NA logic, so a predicate may return null for NA. With no columns selected, if_any() is false and if_all() is true, as in dplyr 1.1. pick(...) returns the selected columns of the current group as a table, for use inside closures.

Results
Each function returns phit’s result array in place of a table, so it ends a method chain. columns holds R’s coefficient names, in R’s order, and coefficients, std_errors, p_values, and conf_int follow the same order. The array also has the fitted values, residuals, fit statistics such as r_squared and sigma, and n_observations and n_dropped, which count the rows used and the rows dropped for missing values.

PHP 8.5+PHP 8.3–8.4


$fit = DataFrame::fromCsv('schools.csv') |&gt;
    filter(fn ($r) =&gt; $r-&gt;prior_score &gt; 50) |&gt;
    lm('score ~ study_hours + prior_score');

foreach (['(Intercept)', 'study_hours', 'prior_score'] as $i =&gt; $term) {
    printf("%-12s %8.4f  (se %.4f)\n", $term, $fit['coefficients'][$i], $fit['std_errors'][$i]);
}
printf("R² = %.4f, n = %d\n", $fit['r_squared'], $fit['n_observations']);

$logit = DataFrame::fromCsv('learning.csv') |&gt; glm('passed ~ study_hours + practice_score', family: 'binomial');
echo 'logit coefficients: ', implode(', ', array_map(fn ($b) =&gt; round($b, 4), $logit['coefficients'])), "\n";


$fit = phplyr(DataFrame::fromCsv('schools.csv'))
    -&gt;filter(fn ($r) =&gt; $r-&gt;prior_score &gt; 50)
    -&gt;lm('score ~ study_hours + prior_score');

foreach (['(Intercept)', 'study_hours', 'prior_score'] as $i =&gt; $term) {
    printf("%-12s %8.4f  (se %.4f)\n", $term, $fit['coefficients'][$i], $fit['std_errors'][$i]);
}
printf("R² = %.4f, n = %d\n", $fit['r_squared'], $fit['n_observations']);

$logit = phplyr(DataFrame::fromCsv('learning.csv'))-&gt;glm('passed ~ study_hours + practice_score', family: 'binomial');
echo 'logit coefficients: ', implode(', ', array_map(fn ($b) =&gt; round($b, 4), $logit['coefficients'])), "\n";



