A first pipeline
The script below reads a CSV file of test scores from 250 students in 12 schools. It keeps the students who studied at least five hours, summarizes each school, and prints the five schools with the highest average score.
To run it, create a Composer project in an empty directory and download the data:
composer require phpstats/phplyr
curl -O https://raw.githubusercontent.com/phpstats/phplyr/v0.4.3/docs/data/schools.csv
Save the script as first.php in the same directory and run php first.php. The “PHP 8.5+” version uses the pipe operator |&gt;. The “PHP 8.3–8.4” version is the same pipeline as a method chain and runs on PHP 8.3 and later.

PHP 8.5+PHP 8.3–8.4


&lt;?php

require __DIR__.'/vendor/autoload.php';

use Phibble\DataFrame;
use function Phplyr\{filter, group_by, summarize, arrange, head, desc, n, mean, sd};

$schools = DataFrame::fromCsv('schools.csv');

echo $schools |&gt;
    filter(fn ($r) =&gt; $r-&gt;study_hours &gt;= 5) |&gt;
    group_by('school') |&gt;
    summarize(students: n(), avg_score: mean('score'), sd_score: sd('score')) |&gt;
    arrange(desc('avg_score')) |&gt;
    head(5);


&lt;?php

require __DIR__.'/vendor/autoload.php';

use Phibble\DataFrame;
use function Phplyr\{phplyr, desc, n, mean, sd};

$schools = DataFrame::fromCsv('schools.csv');

echo phplyr($schools)
    -&gt;filter(fn ($r) =&gt; $r-&gt;study_hours &gt;= 5)
    -&gt;groupBy('school')
    -&gt;summarize(students: n(), avg_score: mean('score'), sd_score: sd('score'))
    -&gt;arrange(desc('avg_score'))
    -&gt;head(5);



