This example adds each order’s customer details from a second table.
Prerequisites: PHP 8.3 or later and composer require phpstats/phplyr. The pipe version needs PHP 8.5. See Installation.
Both tables are created inline. Save the script as example.php in the project directory and run php example.php.

PHP 8.5+PHP 8.3–8.4


&lt;?php

require 'vendor/autoload.php';

use Phibble\DataFrame;
use function Phplyr\left_join;

$orders = DataFrame::fromRows([
    ['order' =&gt; 1, 'customer_id' =&gt; 'c1', 'amount' =&gt; 25.00],
    ['order' =&gt; 2, 'customer_id' =&gt; 'c2', 'amount' =&gt; 12.50],
