The first argument of a vector helper is the column. It can be a column name, col('x'), another helper, or a row closure. Later arguments are values, so a string there is a literal. Wrap a string in col() to refer to a column.
A third form, col('x')-&gt;mul(2), builds an expression. Expressions give the same results as the helpers in memory, and they let a pipeline run as SQL on a database table. See Databases and expressions.

Database tables
Phibble\tbl($pdo, 'table') returns a lazy table for a PDO connection. phplyr functions with expression arguments add to a SQL query instead of loading rows. show_query() returns the SQL, and collect() runs it and returns a DataFrame. SQLite, PostgreSQL, and MySQL are supported.

PHP 8.5+PHP 8.3–8.4


// Load the schools data into an in-memory SQLite database.
$pdo = new PDO('sqlite::memory:');
$pdo-&gt;exec('CREATE TABLE schools (school TEXT, study_hours REAL, prior_score REAL, score REAL)');
$insert = $pdo-&gt;prepare('INSERT INTO schools VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)');
foreach (DataFrame::fromCsv('schools.csv')-&gt;toRows() as $row) {
    $insert-&gt;execute(array_values($row));
}

// The same functions build a query. Nothing runs until collect().
$query = tbl($pdo, 'schools') |&gt;
    filter(col('study_hours')-&gt;ge(5)) |&gt;
    group_by('school') |&gt;
    summarize(students: n(), avg_score: mean('score')) |&gt;
    filter(col('students')-&gt;ge(12)) |&gt;
    arrange(desc('avg_score'));

echo $query |&gt; show_query(), "\n\n";
echo $query |&gt; collect();


// Load the schools data into an in-memory SQLite database.
$pdo = new PDO('sqlite::memory:');
$pdo-&gt;exec('CREATE TABLE schools (school TEXT, study_hours REAL, prior_score REAL, score REAL)');
$insert = $pdo-&gt;prepare('INSERT INTO schools VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)');
foreach (DataFrame::fromCsv('schools.csv')-&gt;toRows() as $row) {
    $insert-&gt;execute(array_values($row));
}

// The same functions build a query. Nothing runs until collect().
$query = phplyr(tbl($pdo, 'schools'))
    -&gt;filter(col('study_hours')-&gt;ge(5))
    -&gt;groupBy('school')
    -&gt;summarize(students: n(), avg_score: mean('score'))
    -&gt;filter(col('students')-&gt;ge(12))
    -&gt;arrange(desc('avg_score'))
    -&gt;get();

echo phplyr($query)-&gt;showQuery(), "\n\n";
echo phplyr($query)-&gt;collect();



