List-columns
A list element is a PHP array. A list is R’s unnamed list or vector, and an array with string keys is a named list.







Function
Use




unnest_wider(col, namesSep:)
One column per name; unnamed elements need namesSep


unnest_longer(col, valuesTo:, indicesTo:, indicesInclude:, keepEmpty:)
One row per element, with names or positions in {col}_id


hoist(col, name: path, _remove:)
Pull components out by name, 1-based position, or a list path


chop(cols), unchop(cols, keepEmpty:)
Collapse rows into list-columns and back


pack(name: cols, _namesSep:), unpack(cols, namesSep:)
Columns into a column of named arrays and back



chop, pack, unpack, and extract share names with PHP built-ins, so import them with use function Phplyr\{chop, pack, unpack, extract};.

