Binding
bind_rows() stacks tables under the input one, matching columns by name and filling missing columns with NA. _id: adds a column with each row’s source. bind_cols() puts tables side by side and renames duplicate names as name...position.

PHP 8.5+PHP 8.3–8.4


$a = DataFrame::fromRows([['id' =&gt; 1, 'v' =&gt; 'a']]);
$b = DataFrame::fromRows([['id' =&gt; 2, 'w' =&gt; true]]);

echo $a |&gt; bind_rows($b, _id: 'source');
echo "\n", $a |&gt; bind_cols(DataFrame::fromRows([['id' =&gt; 10]]));


$a = DataFrame::fromRows([['id' =&gt; 1, 'v' =&gt; 'a']]);
$b = DataFrame::fromRows([['id' =&gt; 2, 'w' =&gt; true]]);

echo phplyr($a)-&gt;bindRows($b, _id: 'source');
echo "\n", phplyr($a)-&gt;bindCols(DataFrame::fromRows([['id' =&gt; 10]]));



